OL,3,GNEWSANew chapter for city's last       
OL,4,Apenmaker                               
OL,6,FBirmingham was once the world's        
OL,7,Fpenmaking capital, home to 127         
OL,8,Fmanufacturers whose parts found their  
OL,9,Fway into writing instruments across the
OL,10,Fglobe. But today, only one site        
OL,11,Fremains.                               
OL,13,FYard-O-Led, a company dating back to   
OL,14,F1822, has opened a new factory in the  
OL,15,Fcity's Jewellery Quarter, where it     
OL,16,Fplans to train apprentices and preserve
OL,17,Ftraditional craftsmanship.             
OL,23,APub: 22-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
